## What #4471 holds

The desk's own view of the ticket, counted from the export:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The two problems

**Day and month swapped: [ticket #1](https://github.com/frameiteasy/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1).**
Booked 2 March, invited for 3 February. Every tenant on file writes the day first, and the date
is read month first. The table splits these reports into `parser` and `hint` by tenant and
channel, but both rows show the same thing, and the reporters cannot tell which way in they
used. One problem, one ticket: it covers both rows. Whoever fixes it checks both the shared
parser and the booking-v3 form's `MM/DD/YYYY` hint.

**The date moves by one day: [ticket #3](https://github.com/frameiteasy/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3).**
Tuesday 12 May shows as Monday 11 May; a client in Lisbon gets Tuesday and a client in Toronto
gets Monday for the same meeting; an invite arrives before the booking. Nothing is swapped.
These are the reports the note under the table counts as read as a one-day move
(`desk-notes.json`). The desk files them under `parser` by tenant, but they point at time zones,
not at date order, and the parser fix will not close them.

## How they were counted

- With the desk's own view, as exported: one report per id, by tenant and channel.
- Not by intake's tag: intake guesses from the reporter's browser, and the table shows how often
  it disagrees.
- Not by subject: the same subject line covers both problems
  ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on subject alone; that is how
  both ended up in one ticket).
- Every number on this page is computed from the export when the page renders.

